# Ship-Safe / “Big Change Won’t Break” Requirements

Code must be resilient to refactors and large updates.

Rules:
- Prefer stable APIs between modules
- Defensive programming: validate inputs, fail gracefully
- Meaningful warnings/errors
- Add debug flags / verification logs for core systems
- Ensure systems work even if optional subsystems are disabled
- Provide sanity checks for each major system

Never claim a feature is implemented unless it’s wired and verifiable at runtime.
